{"book":10,"chapter":17,"context":{"chapter":17,"title":"Counsel Against Counsel","summary":"Ahithophel urges Absalom to strike David at once while he is weary. Hushai flatters Absalom into a slower plan, and Absalom chooses it. Warned in time, David crosses the Jordan; Ahithophel goes home and hangs himself, and friends east of the Jordan supply David's people.","background":"The narrator explains the turn: 'the Lord had appointed to defeat the good counsel of Ahithophel' (v. 14), an answer to David's prayer in 15:31. David's helpers at Mahanaim include Shobi, son of the Ammonite king Nahash, and Machir, who had sheltered Mephibosheth (9:4).","customs":[{"term":"A bear robbed of her whelps","verses":"17:8","note":"A proverbial picture of fierce anger (compare Proverbs 17:12). Hushai uses it to make Absalom fear attacking David quickly."}],"watchFor":["Hushai appeals to Absalom's pride: 'thou go to battle in thine own person' (v. 11).","Two messengers hide in a well under a covering of grain (vv. 18–20).","Help comes from unexpected people (vv. 27–29)."],"connections":["2 Samuel 15:31","Psalms 33:10","Proverbs 17:12","Matthew 27:5"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיֹּאמֶר","vaiyomer","H559","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he said"],["אֲחִיתֹפֶל","'achitofel","H302","HNpm","Ahithophel"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["אַבְשָׁלֹם","'avshalom","H53","HNpm","Absalom"],["אֶבְחֲרָה","'evcharah","H977","HVqc1cs","let me choose"],["נָּא","na'","H4994","HTj","please"],["שְׁנֵים","sheneim-","H8147","HNcbda","two [plus]"],["עָשָׂר","'asar","H6240","HNcbsa","ten"],["אֶלֶף","'elef","H505","HNcbsa","thousand"],["אִישׁ","'ish","H376","HNcmsa","man"],["וְאָקוּמָה","ve'akumah","H6965","HC/Vqc1cs","and I will arise"],["וְאֶרְדְּפָה","ve'erdefah","H7291","HC/Vqc1cs","and I will pursue"],["אַחֲרֵי","'acharei-","H310","HAcmpc","after"],["דָוִד","david","H1732","HNpm","David"],["הַלָּיְלָה","halayelah","H3915","HTd/Ncmsa","this night"]],"x":[[23059007,23059008,5],[19003003,19003005,4],[19004008,19004008,4],